    description: "Becky Chambers' A Psalm for the Wild-Built is the first book in the Monk and Robot series — a gentle, philosophical science fiction novella about Sibling Dex, a monk who travels by wagon to serve tea and listen to people's problems, who finds themselves craving something they can't name. On a solo journey into the uninhabited wilderness, Dex encounters Mosscap, a robot — robots who were given their freedom decades ago and have been living in the woods ever since — who has returned to ask humans what they need. If the warmth, the philosophical questions asked without demanding philosophical answers, and the world that has figured out sustainability gripped you, these eight picks go to the same place.",
