    description: "Evan Winter's The Rage of Dragons is the first book in The Burning duology — an African-inspired epic fantasy that follows Tau Solarin, a young man of the Lower Caste in the Omehi, a people constantly at war with the Hedeni on the continent they invaded. After a massacre that kills everyone he loves, Tau cannot access the magic that protects his people's fighters. He has one advantage: he is willing to train past human endurance, and past human sanity. The world-building draws on Xhosa culture and Zulu history, and the combat is more detailed and more brutal than almost any fantasy novel published in the last decade. If the intensity, the protagonist whose only tool is will, and the world-building rooted in African history gripped you, these eight picks go to the same place.",
