    description: "Blake Crouch's Recursion begins with two parallel storylines: Helena Smith, a neuroscientist working on a machine to help Alzheimer's patients retain their memories, and Barry Sutton, an NYPD detective investigating a new phenomenon called False Memory Syndrome — people suddenly experiencing memories of a completely different life. How these storylines connect is the novel's central revelation. Recursion is a thriller that uses the concept of memory and time to ask what we would actually do if we could return to the moment we lost the thing that mattered most — and what that return might cost. If the time-loop premise, the momentum, and the emotional weight of the central relationship gripped you, these eight picks go to the same place.",
